WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:07.125
First: an enabled Active Directory
account has had no logon for ninety days.

3
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:08.387
What does the code do?

4
00:00:08.387 --> 00:00:09.612
The answer is b.

5
00:00:09.612 --> 00:00:14.098
It raises a stale lead, N P I I N
V oh two, to confirm against the

6
00:00:14.098 --> 00:00:19.051
domain controller and Entra sign-in
logs, and it changes nothing.

7
00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:21.159
A stale account is only a lead,

8
00:00:21.159 --> 00:00:25.112
and the code never disables,
moves or deletes anything.

9
00:00:25.112 --> 00:00:31.150
Second: j doe is high risk, and
also carries N P I I N V oh eight.

10
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.338
Why does that matter?

11
00:00:32.338 --> 00:00:33.474
The answer is a.

12
00:00:33.474 --> 00:00:36.782
It was found only by a
password that never expires,

13
00:00:36.782 --> 00:00:39.525
so it may be a person,
not a service account.

14
00:00:39.525 --> 00:00:41.565
Learn's criteria can find people too,

15
00:00:41.565 --> 00:00:45.713
